                            <comment id="16439602" author="ivandasch" created="Mon, 16 Apr 2018 15:43:38 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Number of retries and timeout between retries are hardcoded in GridClientAbstractProjection, 3 and 1000ms respectively. This affects therefore all GridClientCompute invocations, not only control.sh. I suggest to introduce new System properties: i.e IGNITE_GRID_CLIENT_COMPUTE_RECONNECT_TIMEOUT and IGNITE_GRID_CLIENT_COMPUTE_NUM_RETRIES.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16439724" author="githubbot" created="Mon, 16 Apr 2018 17:04:19 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;GitHub user ivandasch opened a pull request:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/3835&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/3835&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-7786&quot; title=&quot;Changing baseline topology on cluster may have error in control.sh utility&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-7786&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-7786&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; Add ping timeout and ping interval to control.sh. Also,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    make default values greater.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You can merge this pull request into a Git repository by running:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    $ git pull &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ivandasch/ignite&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/ivandasch/ignite&lt;/a&gt; ignite-7786&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Alternatively you can review and apply these changes as the patch at:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/3835.patch&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/3835.patch&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;To close this pull request, make a commit to your master/trunk branch&lt;br/&gt;
with (at least) the following in the commit message:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    This closes #3835&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;commit ac53a778abbb4b4d4b0d19d71bdff36593d0c3ac&lt;br/&gt;
Author: Ivan Daschinskiy &amp;lt;ivandasch@...&amp;gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Date:   2018-04-16T17:03:32Z&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-7786&quot; title=&quot;Changing baseline topology on cluster may have error in control.sh utility&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-7786&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-7786&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; Add ping timeout and ping interval to control.sh. Also,&lt;br/&gt;
    make default values greater.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;hr /&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16440953" author="dpavlov" created="Tue, 17 Apr 2018 14:51:40 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Is this new timeout applied only to baseline change or other actions?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16440980" author="ivandasch" created="Tue, 17 Apr 2018 15:05:31 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Yes, to all actions. But user can specify these params by himself using cmd params.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16440986" author="ivandasch" created="Tue, 17 Apr 2018 15:08:15 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I implements a little bit different idea. I use GridClientConfiguration plus I fixed U.currentTimeMillies() issue thanks to&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=macrergate&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;macrergate&quot;&gt;macrergate&lt;/a&gt;. I think a new approach is better.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16441025" author="dpavlov" created="Tue, 17 Apr 2018 15:31:35 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Thank you, I&apos;ve looked to these changes and I can suggest improving javadoc, probably all methods and fields may have javadoc like&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
@param pingInterval See {@link GridClientConfiguration#PING_INTERVAL}.&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It is not too hard to implement and will allow other Igniters to &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;alternate&quot; type=&quot;square&quot;&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;easily serf in code base&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;will avoid question like where this field is used.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</comment>
                            <comment id="16441030" author="dpavlov" created="Tue, 17 Apr 2018 15:33:06 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Could you please link ticket to its TC run?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16441040" author="ivandasch" created="Tue, 17 Apr 2018 15:40:22 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Sure, a little bit later.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16442007" author="ivandasch" created="Wed, 18 Apr 2018 07:07:12 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=dpavlov&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;dpavlov&quot;&gt;dpavlov&lt;/a&gt; Tests seems to be ok for me.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16442442" author="dpavlov" created="Wed, 18 Apr 2018 12:48:13 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=ivandasch&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;ivandasch&quot;&gt;ivandasch&lt;/a&gt;, unfortunately TC build is outdated. I can see new commits after run.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Example&#160;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-8021&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-8021&lt;/a&gt;&#160;showed us it is too dangerious to accept outdated TC runs because in general we cant be sure new commits are safe.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Moreover I prefer to always use run-all. Community some time ago agreed that we remove commit-based run-all from master. Instead of this we use run-all for PR and check these runs result. We can suppose RunAll is not needed for this change, but in the same time we could run RunAll basic or BinaryObject Simple mapper basic, etc.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16442472" author="ivandasch" created="Wed, 18 Apr 2018 13:12:57 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=dpavlov&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;dpavlov&quot;&gt;dpavlov&lt;/a&gt; I understand your concerns. I will merge latest changes and rerun run-all asap&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16443764" author="ivandasch" created="Thu, 19 Apr 2018 09:04:04 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=dpavlov&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;dpavlov&quot;&gt;dpavlov&lt;/a&gt; Run-all results are ready and they are ok for me.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16443838" author="dpavlov" created="Thu, 19 Apr 2018 10:21:43 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=ivandasch&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;ivandasch&quot;&gt;ivandasch&lt;/a&gt;, TC looks as red as usual and there is no suspicious failures.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16448453" author="dmitriygovorukhin" created="Mon, 23 Apr 2018 17:04:24 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Looks good for me, please merge.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16448571" author="agura" created="Mon, 23 Apr 2018 17:48:49 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Merged to master branch. Thanks for contribution!&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
